Error [E0746]: `fs.read` has the `Fs` effect, which can't be rolled back inside a `#Transact` block
  --> tests/ui/transact_irreversible_effect.jet:5:20
    |
  5 |         text :: fs.read("ledger.txt") ?? "missing"
    |                    ^^^^
 Why: a `#Transact` block undoes its work on a `?`-failure; a network, file, or subprocess effect (`Fs`) leaves committed external state a rollback can't take back
 Fix: move this call after the block, or register it with `<handle>.on_commit(() => { … })` so it runs only on a clean commit
